{
 "summary": "The evidence does not explain the reported checkout outage. Gateway, orders and inventory all show 0% 5xx and normal p95 latency (≤182ms) across the window, while traces, logs and deployment records returned nothing. The failure is either outside these services or in a signal the snapshot does not capture, such as 4xx errors, client/edge failures or an unmetered payment or checkout service. No root cause can be assigned yet.",
 "root_cause": null,
 "contributing_factors": [],
 "timeline": [],
 "ruled_out": [
  {
   "statement": "Server-side 5xx errors or latency at the gateway are not the cause: the gateway 5xx ratio was 0% (max 0%) and p95 latency averaged 136ms (max 182ms).",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-be0e298b6f6f"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Failures or a timeout cascade in orders and inventory are not supported: both had a 0% 5xx ratio and flat p95 latency (orders max 100ms, inventory max 47ms).",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-ec0b0895dc48",
    "ev-5859ba914c39"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "No deployment is recorded in the window, so there is no deploy lead. This is an empty query result, not proof that nothing changed.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "src-deployments"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "unknowns": [
  "Whether customer checkout requests reach the gateway at all. The gateway still serves about 1.95 req/s (last 1.56 req/s), but there is no baseline to judge whether traffic dropped, which would point to DNS, CDN, load balancer or client-side failure.",
  "The metrics cover only the 5xx ratio. 4xx responses (auth, validation, rate limiting) could break checkout without showing here.",
  "Whether a payment or checkout-specific service exists that is not covered by these metrics.",
  "Traces and logs returned nothing even though all three services carried traffic, which suggests an instrumentation or ingestion gap rather than true absence.",
  "No deployment records exist for the window. Config, feature-flag or third-party (payment provider) changes would not appear in this snapshot.",
  "Which endpoints the measured request rates represent, for example whether checkout/POST routes are included or only health and read traffic."
 ],
 "recommended_actions": [
  {
   "action": "Reproduce the failure with a synthetic or manual checkout and capture the exact client-visible error and HTTP status.",
   "rationale": "The server-side metrics show no failures, so the observed symptom must be confirmed and localized first.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-be0e298b6f6f"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Query gateway metrics broken down by route and status code, including 4xx, for checkout endpoints, and compare request rate against the prior day or week.",
   "rationale": "Only aggregate 5xx ratio and rate are available. A checkout-specific 4xx spike or a traffic drop would be hidden.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-be0e298b6f6f"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Check the edge layer (DNS, CDN, load balancer or ingress) and the frontend for errors or a traffic drop before requests reach the gateway.",
   "rationale": "The backend services look healthy, so failures upstream of the gateway would match a full outage with clean backend metrics.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-be0e298b6f6f",
    "ev-ec0b0895dc48",
    "ev-5859ba914c39"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Re-run the trace and log queries with a wider window and verify the collectors and ingestion pipelines are working.",
   "rationale": "Empty traces and logs despite live traffic likely point to a telemetry gap, and that data is needed to find the failure.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "src-traces",
    "src-logs"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Check for config, feature-flag, secret or payment-provider changes outside the deployment records, and check the payment provider's status.",
   "rationale": "The deployment records are empty, and a non-deploy change or third-party outage would not appear in this snapshot.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "src-deployments"
   ]
  }
 ]
}
